WEBVTT

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.790
I said I'm sorry!

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:16.540
Natsusa-<i>san</i>! I'm very sorry!

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:20.750
But we thought it would be better if
the two of you practiced alone...

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.660
I'm not mad at you, Yuu.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:26.250
It must have been scary to
suddenly be taken away by car!

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:29.410
But thank goodness it looks like
he got his touch back...

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:36.330
Looks like everyone else is
completely out of touch, though?

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.540
What is with those terrible t-shirts?

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:38.870
"Chicken Tempura"
What is with those terrible t-shirts?

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:39.290
"Chicken Tempura"
You'll keep messing up as long as you
wear them. You are, even in this moment.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:43.120
You'll keep messing up as long as you
wear them. You are, even in this moment.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.410
Oh, wow. You're in such a bad mood.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.040
But, well...

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.000
I'm glad we came.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.160
Don't touch me so casually.

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.370
What are you being so smug about?

00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:08.660
Don't act like some kind of intellectual
character that helped in the background.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:13.580
What are you doing?!
There's no time to be mad!

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.830
We have to go home tomorrow.

00:01:15.830 --> 00:01:19.700
We still haven't gone to the one place
that Oita is famous for!

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.290
Hurry up!

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.370
Thank goodness.

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:28.950
I'm glad I prayed that Natsusa wouldn't
be too mean to me at the shrine...

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.540
God...

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:33.160
Thank you very much.

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:36.370
You came all the way to Oita
and prayed for something like that?

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:11.870
"Carbonic acid hot springs aren't too hot,
so you can stay in them a long time."
"Shuwa Shuwa Hot Springs"

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:14.290
"Carbonic acid hot springs aren't too hot,
so you can stay in them a long time."
"Shuwa Shuwa Hot Springs"
Wow! So this is Shuwa Shuwa Hot Springs!

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:15.580
"Shuwa Shuwa Hot Springs"
Wow! So this is Shuwa Shuwa Hot Springs!

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:19.910
Oh, the temperature is pretty low.

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:23.910
Well, the temperature is a little lower
because it's a carbonated hot spring.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.540
I see!

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:28.120
If you wait a bit,
something interesting will happen.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:31.330
Huh? What's going to happen? I can't wait!

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:34.540
Whoa! Natsusa! Your wound is super red!

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:37.660
Oh, yeah.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:42.290
If I take a bath or drink alcohol and
my body temperature rises, it turns red.

00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:43.790
Isn't it cool?

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.660
The scar throbs when you get close
to your arch nemesis, right?

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:50.370
Right! It throbs when a certain
shallow man, my arch nemesis, is nearby!

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:53.620
If that's the case, it throbs the whole
time you're in the rugby club, right?

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:55.540
Oh, you can tell?

00:03:56.450 --> 00:04:02.000
He's so indifferent that you can't tell
he can't play rugby because of that injury...

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:03.700
Huh?!

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:07.330
He changed from player
to manager so fast, too.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:09.370
Oh, yes...

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:11.080
What about you?

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:14.410
Have you really accepted the fact
that you couldn't be a player?

00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:17.000
Huh? I...

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:22.910
I was jealous of the players in the beginning...

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.790
But...

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.910
After trying my best at being a manager,

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:32.200
I feel like the work suits me very much
and I'm enjoying myself a lot right now!

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:36.000
I'm really glad I became a manager!

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.540
I see.

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:41.120
But I wonder about Natsusa-<i>san</i>?

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:45.200
He always looks so calm,
so I can't really tell...

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.370
I wonder if I can support him somehow!

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:51.580
Natsusa is shorter than us, right?

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:55.830
In the past, he couldn't
reach toys in high places.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:57.040
Huh?

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:02.250
He'd get mad when Seiichirou
or I grabbed it for him.

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:05.040
"I can get it myself!"

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:07.830
That attitude of his still hasn't changed.

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:15.290
That's why Seiichirou and I don't help him
unless he asks for help.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:22.250
I believe that Natsusa's the type that
can get the toys he wants himself.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:27.120
And I believe he's the type who will
ask for help when he really needs it.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:29.200
You should wait for him, too.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:31.580
Yes!

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:35.040
Take a look at your body, Yuu-<i>kun</i>.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:39.120
Wow! Amazing!

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.120
Oh! Look at this, Yasunari-<i>kun</i>!

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:43.540
I'm covered in bubbles!

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:45.500
Is that really that amazing?

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:48.750
It is! I've never been in
a hot spring like this before!

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:49.160
"Yuu"
It is! I've never been in
a hot spring like this before!

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:52.580
"Yuu"
Look, I can write my name!

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:57.500
I can't believe you tried to become
a rugby player with such a skinny body...

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.540
S-Sorry!

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:06.120
You can write on your body!

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:11.620
Don't worry! I'll turn a cutie like you
into a muscular man!

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:13.120
I'll draw them on!

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.000
No! It's more like this!

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.910
That tickles!

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:21.160
Ripped! Totally ripped!

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:22.750
Wow! Amazing!

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:25.040
It really looks like I have a six-pack!

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:28.450
Look! Everyone is so good at drawing!

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.540
It disappeared...

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:36.250
Of course.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.540
--I'll draw on you, too, Yasunari!
--Wait!

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:42.200
Then, I'll draw wings on his back
like he has 8th grader syndrome.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:43.040
--How many do you want?
--Ibuki-<i>san</i>.

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:43.660
--How many do you want?
--Huh?

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:44.620
--All right! Let's do this!
--Huh?

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:46.750
--All right! Let's do this!
--There's a moth there.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:51.580
What the hell? What's he screaming for?

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:54.040
Moth! There! There's a moth there!

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.790
Huh?! Gross!

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:56.790
Where is it?

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:58.870
Yasunari, is it alive? Is it alive?!

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:01.160
It's not a moth. It's just a fallen leaf.

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:02.580
Huh? Really?

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:05.500
There's no way a moth would
be around this time of the year.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:09.370
I'm sorry. I took out my contacts
and it looked like a moth to me.

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:11.410
Take a closer look.

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.790
Don't joke around! I'll kill you!

00:07:13.790 --> 00:07:16.160
Shut up. It's just a moth.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.500
Whose fault is that?!

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:23.080
You're the one who traumatized me
by putting one in my underwear!

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:25.250
That's really terrible...

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.580
I mistook it for a butterfly.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:31.580
Even so, you shouldn't drop bugs
in other people's underwear!

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:36.950
Gakuto, aren't you going to
get in the hot spring?

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:41.410
I'm going to stay in here
until it gets less noisy out there.

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:42.910
Same.

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:45.040
Sorry for causing you trouble this time.

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:47.370
Hm? What do you mean?

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:48.540
Nothing...

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:53.120
Even so, you really love saunas.

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:57.330
Do you remember that serious fight in
the sauna when we were first-year students?

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:59.750
We were so young then.

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:02.500
That was pretty dangerous,
now that I think about it.

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:04.950
You're the one who picked a fight with me.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:09.200
Well, you pissed me off because you
acted like you were captain or something.

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.330
I wasn't acting like one.

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:15.620
I know. You've always had
a captain-like personality.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:18.160
I could never win against you.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:21.750
But I didn't realize that at the time.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:27.580
Are you really going to quit rugby
when you graduate?

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:29.410
I am.

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:33.830
Do you know why I gave up going pro?

00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:35.660
No...

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:39.620
It's because I believe I've already met
the best captain I could meet.

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.660
I'm satisfied.

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:46.040
There isn't a captain better than you.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:48.580
I think that would be the same
even if I went pro.

00:08:48.580 --> 00:08:51.540
But are there better players than me?

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.450
Yeah, there are.

00:08:53.450 --> 00:08:55.120
--That's not...
--It's true.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:09:00.540
I'm confident in my abilities to judge people.
That's why I know myself well.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:05.080
You're going higher. You're not
the type to be satisfied here.

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:09.290
But someone like me, who is satisfied,
can no longer keep up with you.

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:14.870
That's why I know. It's impossible
that you'd lose in the Kansai League.

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:19.120
You're a man who can
take this team to nationals.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:20.500
I see...

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:26.040
That's right. It seems you're worried
about me and a lot of things right now,

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:29.290
but I want you to only focus on rugby.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:31.410
Got it?

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:33.040
Oh! Gakuto!

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:38.450
There were rugby key holders
at the gift shop earlier! Did you see?

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:41.120
It's the same series that Natsusa has!

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.290
Yeah.

00:09:42.290 --> 00:09:44.040
We should buy them for everyone!

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:47.160
They're so cute, so I've been
wanting them for a while!

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:57.950
What are you looking at?

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:03.950
Oh! You didn't try to contact that woman
who thinks she's a tragic heroine, right?!

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:07.290
Again... You gave a person's mom
such a weird nickname...

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:09.580
But it's the truth!

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:15.410
I didn't contact her, but she contacted me
like she knew I came back to Oita.

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:17.750
This is why I hate the countryside!

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:20.410
Rumors spread like wildfire here!

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:23.000
Don't do it.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.290
Do what?

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:28.410
Don't meet with her. We're already
in a pinch because of our final game.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:30.750
It'll make things more complicated.

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:32.540
I won't meet with her.

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:34.250
Good.

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:37.160
I'm so full!

00:10:37.160 --> 00:10:41.330
You usually don't eat much,
unless it's fruit or sushi...

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:45.410
It's worth treating your junior
when he eats a lot, right?

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:47.540
If he's a cute junior, yeah.

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.410
Cute?

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:52.540
So you want me to tilt my head
and look up at you at the point where

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:57.160
I haven't even finished chewing and
surely don't know how it tastes to say,

00:10:57.160 --> 00:11:01.580
"This is delicious! I've never had
anything so delicious before in my life!"

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:03.160
--Or something? To begin with, Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>...

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:04.120
--Stop!
--Or something? To begin with, Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>...

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:08.200
I don't want to fight! I don't want
to fight! I'm the one in the wrong!

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:10.200
As long as you know.

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:14.700
It's been a long time since
I've slept over at Sei's house.

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:18.700
If you sleep like that,
it'll cause stress on your neck again.

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:27.410
Ibuki-<i>san</i>, do you want to take a bath?

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:29.950
I do. I do. Is your dad
away on business again?

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:30.790
Yes.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:33.700
It'd be too hard to fit three people
at Natsusa's house.

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:36.910
I'm glad that your place was free.

00:11:36.910 --> 00:11:39.830
What? You forgot to reserve a hotel?

00:11:39.830 --> 00:11:41.450
That's a problem...

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:44.370
That's right! Sorry, it slipped my mind.

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:48.580
Oh! But Ibuki and the others
have homes here, right?!

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:50.910
Oh! That's right!

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:56.580
Thanks!

00:11:58.370 --> 00:12:02.790
Sorry, I crumbled against the pressure.

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:04.000
It's fine.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:07.870
So? Did you figure out
what made you nervous?

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:09.580
"Winner"
"Seiichirou Shingyouji-<i>dono</i>"

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.000
"Winner"
"Seiichirou Shingyouji-<i>dono</i>"
That award certificate.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:15.160
"Winner"
"Seiichirou Shingyouji-<i>dono</i>"
Huh? Oh, that. It's always been there.

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:19.120
It is the award certificate from
when I won the school marathon.

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:21.000
Natsu put it up there in the past.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:23.250
I see.

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:28.000
I lived with my workaholic father,
who had no interest in me,

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:32.120
so I didn't know how it felt for someone
to be happy about something I did.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:38.500
I was surprised how happy
Natsu was when I won...

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:41.790
And I never wanted to lose that feeling.

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:48.370
Natsu stopped smiling after that accident.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:54.500
So when he smiled and told me he loved
my conversion kicks, it scared me.

00:12:54.500 --> 00:13:00.450
I started to think that I'd never make
Natsu happy again if I missed the kicks.

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:02.080
There's no way that'd happen.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:07.200
Yes. I was so weighed down with my
earthly desires that I couldn't even see that.

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:09.540
What? Earthly desires?

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:11.950
Sasaki told me.

00:13:11.950 --> 00:13:17.450
Humans have 108 earthly desires
and they suffer because of them.

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:20.660
Among those desires is fixation.

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:23.660
While it's true that it makes me suffer,

00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:27.700
fixation is not all that bad.

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:30.120
I guess so.

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:37.750
I-I'm sorry for the sudden intrusion!

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.000
Um, this isn't much, but...

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.620
Something huge has happened!

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:46.000
Yasunari brought a girlfriend home!

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:47.870
Wait! He's not a girlfriend!

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:51.120
He never even brought a friend home
when he was in high school!

00:13:51.120 --> 00:13:53.040
He had no friends, after all!

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:54.870
Now, now! Come in! Come in!

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:58.410
I'm sorry! If I knew you were coming,
I would have cooked up a feast...

00:13:58.410 --> 00:14:00.450
You idiot! Tell me ahead of time!

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:01.410
Ouch!

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:03.910
Oh! We've already eaten...

00:14:03.910 --> 00:14:07.410
Oh, I see. Then, maybe some tea snacks...

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:08.370
Hey!

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:10.790
Yasunari! Go buy some tea snacks!

00:14:10.790 --> 00:14:12.250
I wonder if it's still open...

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:13.870
He'd be cutting it close...

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:17.160
Hurry up and go, Yasunari!
The bike is right outside!

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:20.080
Um, please don't worry about us...

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:22.330
Also, I'm a man...

00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:23.830
Thank you for coming.

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:27.620
As you can see, our family is like this.

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:30.870
No one is likely to take my older girls.

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:34.330
You and Yasunari are the only ones
who can protect our family grave now!

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:36.910
That's enough!

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.200
Ibuki-<i>chan</i>!

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:03.910
Mom...

00:15:03.910 --> 00:15:06.540
I told you I wouldn't meet you today.

00:15:06.540 --> 00:15:09.330
Is it true that you've started
playing rugby again?!

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:12.450
Yeah, I'm sorry I didn't tell you.

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:15.290
Y-You can't!

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:20.250
You have to study hard at the university
and join your brother's company!

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:22.290
Mom...

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:26.870
I told you many times that
I won't work at his company...

00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:28.950
Don't say something like that!

00:15:28.950 --> 00:15:33.200
If you get along well with your brother,
I'll be treated better!

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:36.580
Please... I can't do anything!

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:39.120
You're the only one
I can depend on, Ibuki-<i>chan</i>.

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:45.120
Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>, it's time. Let's go.

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:48.450
Stop! We weren't done talking!

00:15:48.450 --> 00:15:51.290
Ibuki-<i>chan</i>! Ibuki-<i>chan</i>, wait!

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:52.160
Ibuki-<i>chan</i>!

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:53.750
Natsusa...

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:58.120
Then don't just space out and sit there!

00:15:58.120 --> 00:15:59.950
Come and take him away!

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:01.830
You're always like this!

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:04.000
You never try to do anything on your own!

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:05.950
You use the fact that
you're weak like a weapon!

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:08.790
You're just sitting around and
waiting for Ibuki-<i>senpai </i>to save you!

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:12.750
On top of that, you try to drag him down
when he's trying his best!

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:18.250
I'll never forgive you for what you did
when he got into the university!

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:22.290
There was nothing I could do at the time!

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.910
Mom...

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:26.830
If you want to act like
a tragic heroine, do it alone!

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:30.410
Don't involve Ibuki-<i>senpai </i>any more than this!

00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:31.950
Natsusa...

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:36.700
Natsu.

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:38.620
Seiichirou...

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:40.750
Take Natsusa with you.

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:42.160
Ibuki-<i>senpai</i>!

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:45.040
Don't worry. I'll definitely join you.

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:45.910
Okay?

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:47.250
But!

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:51.410
I promise. It's fine.

00:16:51.410 --> 00:16:53.700
Natsu, let's go.

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:56.330
He's so terrible.

00:16:56.330 --> 00:16:59.540
He doesn't understand how I feel at all!

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:03.200
He doesn't understand
how much I'm suffering!

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:04.500
He does.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:10.160
Mom, Natsusa can't play rugby anymore
because of that accident with me.

00:17:10.160 --> 00:17:11.750
Huh?

00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:15.160
But he's working as the manager
of the rugby club now.

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:17.910
He's amazing.

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:22.870
No matter how hard it is for him,
he boldy goes after what he wants.

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:27.660
He tries to grasp it himself,
no matter what it takes.

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:29.370
But!

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:33.790
There are too many things that
you and I have to give up.

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:37.120
We always say that it "can't be helped"

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:41.040
and think we can't obtain it ourselves.

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:44.080
That's why you try to
depend on me so much, Mom.

00:17:46.000 --> 00:17:49.750
But there's something I want right now.

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:51.950
And something I don't want to lose.

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:54.660
There are things I want to gain back.

00:17:54.660 --> 00:18:00.370
I went to college with those feelings,
but a lot of things happened and I forgot.

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:04.830
I'm going to try giving it another shot.

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:07.200
What about you, Mom?

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:15.200
Even if it doesn't work out, you might
still gain something from not giving up.

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:22.620
Natsusa!

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:26.790
Don't come near me. Lying bastard.

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:30.450
It can't be helped.
She was the one who came to me.

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:32.250
There you go again with excuses!

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.620
Yeah. I won't anymore.

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:41.370
I won't give up or feel sorry for her.

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:42.700
It'll be okay.

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:45.290
Thanks.

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:48.080
I don't need words. Show me
your thanks with your actions.

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:49.700
Yeah. Yeah.

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:56.330
Kotori!

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:58.370
I'm fine.

00:18:58.370 --> 00:18:59.450
Are we going to keep going?

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:01.370
We are!

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:04.040
I haven't done any
step practice yet, either!

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:05.120
But...

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:10.160
We have to fill the space Taku-<i>senpai</i>
left behind! I have to do something about it!

00:19:10.160 --> 00:19:12.450
We can't lose!

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:15.160
I have to be able to do passes and attacks!

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:16.000
But...

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:18.580
If you don't want to do it with me, go home!

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:29.540
What? Going shopping?

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:30.790
That's right.

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:34.950
Since Taisei-<i>senpai </i>is busy
taking care of Hidaka-<i>senpai</i>,

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:39.290
Li-<i>san </i>said he'd do the shopping
and we're showing him the way.

00:19:39.290 --> 00:19:40.830
To Torriere?

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:42.910
Yes. You, as well?

00:19:42.910 --> 00:19:44.370
Y-Yeah...

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:45.750
I see.

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:47.290
Well, then. I'll...

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:50.790
Hm? You are going to the same place?

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:53.830
Did I confuse my Japanese?

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:54.950
It's right.

00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:58.000
Then, why are we not going together?

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.750
Th-Then should we go together?

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:03.750
You want to? That's unusual...

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:06.450
It can't be helped.
I have to act like we get along.

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:09.700
If Sousuke-<i>senpai </i>or
Syouta-<i>senpai </i>find out about this,

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:15.620
they'll egg us on to kiss and
make up again. Seriously...

00:20:15.620 --> 00:20:20.160
I wish they didn't think that people from
the same school automatically get along.

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:22.000
People like Natsu-<i>san </i>and Seiichirou

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:26.120
or Uchinashi-<i>senpai</i>
and Takumi-<i>san </i>are special.

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:31.200
Hey, why are there people sitting in such
an organized fashion under the bridge?

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:32.540
Is it some kind of event?

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:33.950
Hm?

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:35.660
Oh, that's not it.

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:37.910
This is a holy land for couples.

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:41.040
They're sitting there
and talking with each other.

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:42.620
Is it some kind of rule?

00:20:42.620 --> 00:20:43.910
Rule?

00:20:43.910 --> 00:20:46.910
How can they sit at such regular intervals?

00:20:46.910 --> 00:20:48.540
Was that decided ahead of time?

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:50.620
Hm. I wonder why.

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:55.250
Is it the ability to read the atmosphere
that's pretty unique to the Japanese?

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:57.410
Reading the atmosphere! I know about it!

00:20:57.410 --> 00:20:59.950
It's very hard to do...

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:02.700
If they can read the atmosphere,
they shouldn't be there in the first place.

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:07.160
This was a place where they used
to exhibit the heads of the executed.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:11.250
You really know your
Japanese history, Li-<i>senpai</i>...

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:15.120
What are you looking at, Tsuu-<i>san</i>?

00:21:19.870 --> 00:21:23.370
Those five are the ones
who'll end up kissing next time.

00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:32.160
What is it, Yuu?

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:35.450
Yayoi-<i>kun </i>seems to be worried about Kotori-<i>kun</i>.

00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:36.700
Huh?

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:40.120
He didn't rest yesterday and kept practicing.

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:40.750
"Yayoi Tsudura: I think the pressure
from the match is keeping him up."
He didn't rest yesterday and kept practicing.

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:41.330
"Yayoi Tsudura: I think the pressure
from the match is keeping him up."
It seems he spent the night looking at
Kofuuin videos and isn't sleeping much.

00:21:41.330 --> 00:21:42.450
"Yayoi Tsudura: Even after it got dark, he spent
his time watching Kofuuin videos to strategize."
It seems he spent the night looking at
Kofuuin videos and isn't sleeping much.

00:21:42.450 --> 00:21:43.450
"Yayoi Tsudura: We practiced tackling yesterday
even though we were supposed to rest."
It seems he spent the night looking at
Kofuuin videos and isn't sleeping much.

00:21:43.450 --> 00:21:44.370
"Yayoi Tsudura: He keeps saying we have to
fill the space left by Taku-<i>senpai</i>."
It seems he spent the night looking at
Kofuuin videos and isn't sleeping much.

00:21:44.370 --> 00:21:47.250
"Yayoi Tsudura: It's about Kotori."
It seems he spent the night looking at
Kofuuin videos and isn't sleeping much.

00:21:47.250 --> 00:21:51.870
I see. The first match he's joining
as a starter is against Kofuuin, after all.

00:21:51.870 --> 00:21:54.830
It must be a lot of pressure.

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:57.950
I'll talk about it with Taku-<i>senpai</i>.

00:21:57.950 --> 00:21:59.620
Madoka-<i>san</i>?!

00:23:41.950 --> 00:23:43.660
"Chicken tempura tastes the best
